(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "adr-2609160130-kotoba-cloud-code-block-console-locales-closing")
  (:adr/title "kotoba.cloud 2026-09-15/16: readable code blocks (cloud-kotoba-dds.code + shinkansen :code-language), the console documents as locale variant roots, the console chrome in all 22 public locales — session closing")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-09-16")
  (:adr/related (vector "ADR-2609151708" "ADR-2609091700" "ADR-2609160028" "ADR-2608136000" "ADR-2609112300"))
  (:adr/context
  "Owner direction 2026-09-15, one session, four asks in order: (1) the code area on kotoba.cloud/docs was hard to read — fix the component and the syntax highlighting in cloud-kotoba-dds and in the shinkansen web framework; (2) https://kotoba.cloud/account?lang=en still did not switch language — verify by driving Chrome; (3) 'do the rest too, with English translation — and the site used to support Indonesian and the other languages'; (4) 'ok, do it: translate the console to match the landing, an OpenRouter translation API is fine'.

  Measured before any change (curl + Chrome, 2026-09-15 22:1x JST): the docs code block was a bare <pre class=kc-docs__config> styled label-on-system-background, i.e. on the dark theme a bright grey slab with a black border, one colour for everything, the long curl line clipped at the right edge, nothing to copy with; shinkansen.audit had no axis that could see it. /account?lang=en answered <html lang=\"ja\"> with or without a kb_locale cookie: the console was ONE Japanese emit, 'account' sat in locale/shared-prefixes (declared locale-independent) and the Worker route fetched /account/ verbatim, so the switch on the page was a link to itself. The same three-part cause held for /secure/ /models/ /security/ /security/services/ /identity/ (measured en / ja / id / ar cookies: all ja). The landing page carried the 22 public locales (public-locales, ADR-2609091700) but the console chrome (sidebar, top bar, setup chip and banner, account entry, language switch) was authored ja / en only and its selector offered two entries, so /models/?lang=id rendered lang=id around an English console.

  A parallel session landed the /account part of (2) while this session's equivalent branch was passing its gates (PR #204 'one account console document per public locale' + #205, merged 22:29-22:34 JST and deployed); this session's account branch was discarded unpushed rather than merged twice, and the remaining five documents were done on top of that main."
  )
  (:adr/decision
  "1. Code blocks are a design-system pattern, not page CSS: cloud-kotoba-dds.code (0.1.0, kotoba-lang/cloud-kotoba-dds bcdc2b8, then ce8dd64 for catalog/page :nav-label). `tokenize` is a pure rule table per language (bash with the command word, $VAR inside \"…\" and a JSON body inside '{…}'; json/jsonc; clojure; http; text) whose concatenation is the source verbatim (pinned); `block` emits <figure class=ck-code data-lang><figcaption bar + copy control><pre data-lang><code class=language-x>; no highlighter runtime (a script-src 'self' host cannot load one and a document whose colours arrive with a script is not the self-contained shinkansen :document). Syntax colours are DADS ramp steps chosen for AA (>= 4.5:1) on BOTH surfaces (light gray-50 / dark gray-900) and follow jp-go-dds.dark's primitive mirror — no second palette; the bridge's --hig-palette-green (green-700, 3.84 on light) is therefore the fallback and not the value. Wrap is the default (the measured failure was a clipped line; the copy control keeps the unbroken text); :wrap? false scrolls with tabindex=0. The copy control is emitted hidden and revealed only where the clipboard is writable. test/code.mjs measures 390/1440 × light/dark and was shown to fall on a copy without the wrap rule and on a copy using the bridge green.
  2. shinkansen.audit gains :code-language (kotoba-lang/shinkansen bc04afd): every visible <pre> names its language (data-lang on the pre or class=language-x on its <code>); a <pre hidden> is data a script fills and is not counted; scored as the share of blocks that name one; weight 0.05 beside :pre-overflow, which keeps measuring that the block can scroll or wrap. Both directions pinned (8 assertions); coscientist hypothesis row; SPEC round 5.
  3. app-kotoba-cloud (kotoba-lang/app-kotoba-cloud): every docs config block, the models call example and the two apex kc-command blocks are code/block through app-kotoba-cloud.code-block (one home for the copy-control labels); /js/code.js is shipped and loaded on every document; the dead duplicate docs-css in site.cljk is gone. Landed 5f2e6f8f, deployed e1236bef.
  4. Every console document is a locale variant root negotiated by ?lang= / kb_locale / Accept-Language (locale/static-decision) with the locale-free emit English, /ja/ Japanese and every other public locale emitted under its directory with the shell in that locale and the body in English marked lang=en: secure, models, identity, security, security-data, security/services (this session, 0e1d0a54, deployed 7dcb9127) beside account (PR #204). identity left shared-prefixes and its Worker route negotiates through route-static like /account; secure-site / models-site / security-site take a locale; security-services' capability labels and integration note are {:ja :en} maps like :summary (the edge catalog carries both); assets/security-data.js answers in <html lang>. English bodies carry zero Japanese characters apart from the language selector's own 日本語.
  5. The console chrome is in all 22 public locales (b613e437, deployed 188233e9): app-kotoba-cloud.console-locales is the one home — 38 keys authored en / ja (`source`), the other 20 generated into console-copy-generated by scripts/translate-console-copy.cljk over the OpenRouter API (model anthropic/claude-sonnet-5 via OPENROUTER_MODEL, key from the environment; provenance per locale). Machine translation is permitted by ADR-2609091700 and is recorded as native-speaker unverified. The script validates every answer before writing it (every key, no blank, {placeholders} verbatim, 'Kotoba Cloud' and the leading ＋ kept), reads only the first JSON object of a reply and unwraps a mirrored {en, ja, xx} shape — on the first run 14 of 19 locales were rejected and 2 failed to parse for exactly those reasons; --check reports SCANNED 760 / MISSING 0. console.cljk's IA table holds keys, not copy; the console language switch offers every public locale as ?lang= on the same route; shell-browser reads its seven runtime strings from #kc-console-copy data-* in the document's locale, so the document's language is authoritative under a stale bundle. Coverage recorded in 90-docs/reports/260909-public-site-locales.edn under kotoba.cloud :console (a637e187).
  6. (Superseded the same day by decision 7.) Until 2026-09-16 the console BODIES were ja / en only and the other 20 locales got an English body in a localized shell.
  7. The bodies speak every public locale too (owner direction 2026-09-16 '本文も多言語対応'; app-kotoba-cloud ce66187aaa36ffd3a0d4321b605062aa071f08d6, deployed 9493389d-cfaa-48b4-b1f2-3fa1efebb42b). app-kotoba-cloud.copy/txt-for keeps the call sites as (txt \"ja\" \"en\") and answers other locales from a generated map keyed by the ENGLISH string, English per string when the map does not know it; the browser's strings travel in each document as #kc-copy-runtime (<script type=application/json>, keyed by English, `<` escaped) and account-browser / shell-browser / billing-browser / assets/security-data.js read it, so the generated maps (904 KB of source) never enter a bundle (session.js +1 KB). scripts/translate-console-copy.cljk is general: --source over a registry that EXTRACTS the pairs from the source files (literal (txt/t \"ja\" \"en\"), {:ja :en} data, secure.cljk's English-only :description / :note), batches of 40, a failing batch rejects the locale, --check over every source: SCANNED 8540 / MISSING 0 (account 147, secure 46, models 35, security 87, billing 33, site 41 keys × 20 locales). Dynamic browser messages became {placeholder} templates so they translate. billing, apps and security/aup are now emitted for every public locale as well. Not translated on purpose: the AUP's policy lists and the legal documents — owner decision 2026-09-16 'policy, 法的文書などは英語のみで ok': English-only policy / legal text is not a translation gap for kotoba.cloud (the coverage inventory keeps disclosing it as fallback, ADR-2609091700) — and docs.kotoba.cloud (a separate surface, ja / en)."
  )
  (:adr/body
  "## Verification, as run (the branch is not main until the merge sha is named)

  - cloud-kotoba-dds: test/code.mjs (Playwright, BROWSER_CHANNEL=chrome, PLAYWRIGHT_MODULE=root node_modules): PASS 390/light 390/dark 1440/light 1440/dark — no sideways overflow, wrapping block scrollWidth <= clientWidth, scrolling block scrolls + tabindex=0, 9 token classes each a colour of their own and >= 4.5:1, copy control revealed / copies verbatim / says Copied / restores. Falls on the wrap-less copy ('the default block wraps (white-space pre)') and on the bridge-green copy ('.ck-tok-string rgb(29, 139, 86) on rgb(242, 242, 242) reads at 3.84:1'). Merges bcdc2b8, ce8dd64.
  - shinkansen: npm test 105 tests / 289 assertions, 0 failures (was 104 / 281). Merges 2a3519ad, bc04afd5.
  - app-kotoba-cloud, per landing: shinkansen audit (scripts/uiux-audit.cljk --min 80) OVERALL 98.5 → 99.7 with the new axis on the docs landing (:code-language 43 documents → 0, docs pages 96.7 → 100); 99.7 → 98.4 → 98.2 → 98.0 as 22 × 6 console documents were added (the per-document note-density finding on /models/ and /secure/ pre-exists and is counted per locale; no new axis fails); worker smoke green at every landing, the emit-tree sweep growing 7 → 11 variant roots (account apps billing blog docs identity legal models secure security security-data); real-browser arm (test/account-browser.cljk) green at every landing — its 19 hydration waits were raised from 5 s to WAIT (ACCOUNT_WAIT_MS, default 20 s) because load average 190 on this desktop turned a passing arm into a flake (a signed-out reveal measured 5.7 s); kbb -M:test carries main's pre-existing failure set (265 → 274 → 272 as other sessions landed; the two stale account assertions in locale_test were corrected here) with none added by this session.
  - Production, curl: 5 routes × {en, ja, id, ar} cookies, 100 probes, 0 mismatches after propagation (the first ~60 s after a deploy mix the previous version: ar→ja was seen once); /models/?lang=id answers lang=id with sidebar ＋ Mulai / Dokumentasi / Aplikasi / Token API / Registrasi peneliti / Kepatuhan / Layanan keamanan / Akun / Tim / Pembayaran, selector aria-label Bahasa with 21 alternates, in 64 ms. Chrome (claude-in-chrome): /account?lang=en → English, switch to 日本語 → ?lang=ja Japanese, back to English, bare /account stays English by cookie; /secure/?lang=en → 'Security controls', hydration 'Matches the running policy.' / 'Observe mode: off', zero Japanese characters; /models/?lang=id page text shows the Indonesian chrome (a screenshot could not be captured under the machine load).
  - West pins advanced (server-side single-entry commits): 1fd44ff7 (cloud-kotoba-dds bcdc2b8, shinkansen bc04afd, app-kotoba-cloud 5f2e6f8f), ba84c409 (cloud-kotoba-dds ce8dd64, app-kotoba-cloud 0e1d0a54), 1e6de243 (app-kotoba-cloud b613e437); another session has since advanced app-kotoba-cloud to 2296df57.

  ## Not done / known

  - (Done 2026-09-16, decision 7: the console bodies in the 20 other locales.) docs.kotoba.cloud stays ja / en (293 pairs, a separate surface) and the AUP's policy lists stay English by design.
  - Session bundle grew 256.9 → 284.4 KB (75.9 KB gzipped) because the 22-locale map reaches it through console.cljk's require; moving setup-progress / surfaces out of console.cljk would keep the map server-side. Not done; measured.
  - :note-density on /models/ and /secure/ (two lead paragraphs over 120 characters) pre-exists and is now counted once per locale in the audit; the fix is content, not locale.
  - main's pre-existing kbb -M:test failures (public-entry-locales-…, public-identity-…, public-operator-…, homepage-offers-…, japanese-page-…, signed-in-product-links-…, english-page-…, the-hardcoded-selector-…, sidebar-shell-documents-hold-the-floor ×6, docs-documents-live-on-their-own-host) are not this session's and were not fixed; npm run deploy therefore cannot be used as one command — this session deployed by running build → audit → worker smoke → wrangler deploy --env='' by hand, from a checkout equal to origin/main each time (the deploy guard refused once when main had moved 17 commits during a build; the branch was re-merged, rebuilt and re-gated before deploying).
  - ~/.local/bin/amu is a hermes shim shadowing orgs/kotoba-lang/amu/bin/amu; `npm run build` fails through it. Use the absolute path (with KBB_ENGINE set) until the shim is removed.
  - Deploy race, measured at the second closing (2026-09-16): 9493389d (the translated bodies, from ce66187a = origin/main) was overwritten at 19:40Z by 902aaa22, deployed by another session from a checkout at 6b7ecb7b — origin/main as it had fetched it, before ce66187a landed. The deploy guard compares the checkout with the LAST-FETCHED origin/main, so a checkout that fetched, then waited through a build while main moved, still passes; the console served German / Indonesian shells around English bodies for about seven hours. Restored by rebuilding origin/main (ce66187a) and deploying 6be60c50; 0/36 mismatches after. The rule 'the last deployer wins' holds exactly; a guard that re-fetched right before the deploy command would have refused.
  - The edge cache is keyed by URL, not cookie (cf-cache-status HIT on cookie-negotiated documents); the ?lang= switch is URL-keyed and reliable, the cookie path served a previous version's answer for ~60 s after each deploy. Not a bug in the negotiation; noted for anyone measuring right after a deploy.

  ## Resume point (no conversation needed)

  - cd orgs/kotoba-lang/app-kotoba-cloud && git fetch origin && git log --oneline -1 origin/main   (2296df57 or later; this session's last merge is b613e437)
  - kbb --backend sci scripts/translate-console-copy.cljk --check   (expect SCANNED 760 / MISSING 0; --only <code> regenerates one locale, needs OPENROUTER_API_KEY)
  - curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\\n' -H 'Cookie: kb_locale=id' https://kotoba.cloud/models/ && curl -s -H 'Cookie: kb_locale=id' https://kotoba.cloud/models/ | grep -o '<html lang=\"[a-z-]*\"'   (expect id)
  - cd orgs/kotoba-lang/cloud-kotoba-dds && PLAYWRIGHT_MODULE=/Users/junkawasaki/github/com-junkawasaki/node_modules/playwright BROWSER_CHANNEL=chrome node test/code.mjs   (4 PASS lines)
  - curl -s https://kotoba.cloud/js/session.js | grep -c kc-copy-runtime   (expect 1: the live bundle reads the document's runtime strings; 0 means an older tree was deployed over ce66187a again)
  - kbb --backend sci scripts/translate-console-copy.cljk --check   (expect SCANNED 8540 / MISSING 0 over the seven sources; a new (txt \"ja\" \"en\") pair in a body shows up as MISSING × 20 until --source <name> is run with OPENROUTER_API_KEY)
  - curl -s -H 'Cookie: kb_locale=de' https://kotoba.cloud/account/ | grep -o '<h1[^>]*>[^<]*'   (expect Konto)
  - Next increment, if wanted: docs.kotoba.cloud's 293 pairs through the same script (a :docs source over docs_site.cljk), and a native-speaker review pass recorded per locale in the report.

  ## Owner WIP preserved, not touched

  orgs/kotoba-lang/app-kotoba-cloud main checkout (now detached at a commit 50 behind origin/main, switched by another session; earlier on kotoba-proof-biometric-wiring with tracked changes); orgs/kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang and orgs/kotoba-lang/amu tracked changes reported by the SessionStart hook; ~70 worktrees under ~/.gftd/worktrees, ~/Documents/Codex, /private/tmp and /Users/junkawasaki/github/com-junkawasaki-worktrees that belong to other sessions (akc-docs-3, akc-pat-revoke, akc-billing-live, akc-ekyc-card-start, security-services among them); open PRs on kotoba-lang/app-kotoba-cloud that are not this session's. Every worktree this session made (dds-code-block, dds-catalog-nav, shinkansen-code-language, akc-code-block, akc-main-check, akc-main-check2, akc-account-locale, akc-console-locales, akc-console-22, the two root worktrees) is removed and its branch deleted locally and remotely; the one unmerged branch (account-locale, superseded by PR #204) was never pushed.")
))
